1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,410
August twenty twenty-five.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,620
A hundred-year-old church
rolls down a road in Sweden.

3
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:08,150
On two hundred and twenty-four wheels.

4
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,510
Slower than you walk.

5
00:00:09,976 --> 00:00:11,066
And it's not alone.

6
00:00:11,476 --> 00:00:13,966
The whole town behind
it is packing up too.

7
00:00:14,537 --> 00:00:16,807
So why on earth would you move a town?

8
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:18,098
A flood?

9
00:00:18,388 --> 00:00:18,858
Nope.

10
00:00:19,228 --> 00:00:19,738
A war?

11
00:00:20,028 --> 00:00:20,478
No.

12
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:22,838
The problem isn't on the map at all.

13
00:00:23,068 --> 00:00:23,958
It's under it.

14
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,830
This is Kiruna, the
northernmost town in Sweden,

15
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,350
about ninety miles
above the Arctic Circle.

16
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:34,090
Around twenty-three thousand
people, long snowy winters,

17
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:36,690
and a sun that doesn't
set in early summer.

18
00:00:37,237 --> 00:00:39,647
We'll dig into the mountain
that pays for everything,

19
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:43,127
see how you actually move a town,
ride along with that church,

20
00:00:43,337 --> 00:00:45,907
and find out why the
moving isn't over yet.

21
00:00:46,117 --> 00:00:46,727
Let's go!

22
00:00:50,651 --> 00:00:53,001
First, a fun little secret about the name.

23
00:00:53,591 --> 00:00:56,121
Kiruna comes from the Sámi word Giron.

24
00:00:56,411 --> 00:00:59,401
It means ptarmigan, a
chubby snow-white bird.

25
00:00:59,731 --> 00:01:03,041
The Sámi herded reindeer here
long before there was any town.

26
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:06,755
But the town is here because of
the mountain right next door.

27
00:01:07,465 --> 00:01:10,825
Kiirunavaara is basically
a giant slab of iron ore,

28
00:01:10,865 --> 00:01:12,595
tilted down into the ground.

29
00:01:13,127 --> 00:01:17,667
In nineteen hundred, a mining boss named
Hjalmar Lundbohm drew up a plan for a

30
00:01:17,707 --> 00:01:19,417
brand-new town beside it.

31
00:01:19,647 --> 00:01:22,637
Soon a railway linked it to
the port of Narvik in Norway.

32
00:01:23,207 --> 00:01:24,517
Ore out, money in.

33
00:01:25,036 --> 00:01:27,646
And Kiruna still loves a big project.

34
00:01:28,036 --> 00:01:31,286
About twenty-five miles out of
town there's even a space center,

35
00:01:31,476 --> 00:01:35,776
Esrange, where scientists have launched
well over a thousand research rockets and

36
00:01:35,816 --> 00:01:36,306
balloons.

37
00:01:36,856 --> 00:01:38,966
Iron underground, rockets overhead.

38
00:01:39,543 --> 00:01:42,213
Lundbohm didn't want a grim mining camp.

39
00:01:42,463 --> 00:01:45,333
He wanted a real town,
with art, good schools,

40
00:01:45,603 --> 00:01:47,093
and a church people would love.

41
00:01:47,483 --> 00:01:49,573
Hold that thought, we'll come back to it.

42
00:01:49,991 --> 00:01:51,421
Fast forward to today.

43
00:01:51,971 --> 00:01:56,161
That mountain is now the world's
largest underground iron ore mine,

44
00:01:56,371 --> 00:01:58,541
run by the state company LKAB.

45
00:01:59,178 --> 00:02:00,088
And it's enormous.

46
00:02:00,758 --> 00:02:04,898
Every single day, Kiruna digs up enough
iron ore to build about six and a half

47
00:02:04,938 --> 00:02:05,808
Eiffel Towers.

48
00:02:06,238 --> 00:02:06,888
Every day!

49
00:02:07,417 --> 00:02:10,087
The miners work more than
half a mile underground.

50
00:02:10,537 --> 00:02:14,367
That's deeper than two Empire State
Buildings stacked on top of each other.

51
00:02:14,873 --> 00:02:16,843
Down there it's a whole hidden city.

52
00:02:17,353 --> 00:02:21,753
Tunnels wide enough for trucks, giant
elevators that lift forty tonnes of ore at a

53
00:02:21,793 --> 00:02:23,923
time, and trains running in the dark.

54
00:02:24,373 --> 00:02:28,753
Every summer, tourists can even ride a
bus down to a visitor area deep inside the

55
00:02:28,793 --> 00:02:29,203
mountain.

56
00:02:29,808 --> 00:02:30,998
Now here's the catch.

57
00:02:31,328 --> 00:02:34,038
The method they use is
called sublevel caving.

58
00:02:34,728 --> 00:02:39,258
Miners blast the ore from below, and the
rock above simply caves in to fill the gap.

59
00:02:39,708 --> 00:02:41,418
Blasting happens every night.

60
00:02:41,909 --> 00:02:44,479
Deep underground, that's very efficient.

61
00:02:45,029 --> 00:02:48,579
Up on the surface, it means the
ground slowly cracks and sinks.

62
00:02:48,829 --> 00:02:51,039
And this ore body leans toward the town.

63
00:02:51,602 --> 00:02:55,932
So the deeper the mine goes, the closer
the cracks creep to people's homes.

64
00:02:56,462 --> 00:02:59,212
And you can't live on ground
that's slowly breaking apart.

65
00:02:59,728 --> 00:03:03,438
In two thousand four, LKAB
told the town the news.

66
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:07,018
To keep mining, it had to dig
right under the old center.

67
00:03:07,408 --> 00:03:08,978
So Kiruna had a choice.

68
00:03:09,468 --> 00:03:12,718
Close the mine the whole town
lives on, or move the town.

69
00:03:15,227 --> 00:03:16,517
They chose to move.

70
00:03:16,847 --> 00:03:19,567
The new center would be built
about two miles to the east,

71
00:03:19,607 --> 00:03:20,997
on solid ground.

72
00:03:21,546 --> 00:03:23,116
And the bill goes to the mine.

73
00:03:23,646 --> 00:03:25,216
LKAB pays for the move.

74
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,817
So what happens if your
house is in the way?

75
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,097
You get a choice.

76
00:03:29,587 --> 00:03:32,927
Take the market value of your home,
plus twenty-five percent extra,

77
00:03:32,967 --> 00:03:33,957
in cash.

78
00:03:34,287 --> 00:03:36,837
Or get a brand-new house
in the new part of town.

79
00:03:37,382 --> 00:03:39,192
Sounds like a pretty good deal, right?

80
00:03:39,622 --> 00:03:42,172
But imagine leaving the
street you grew up on.

81
00:03:42,302 --> 00:03:44,062
The window you always looked out of.

82
00:03:44,102 --> 00:03:46,272
The corner shop where
everybody knew your name.

83
00:03:46,829 --> 00:03:51,519
In the old center, whole blocks now
stand empty behind tall blue fences,

84
00:03:51,809 --> 00:03:53,159
waiting to be torn down.

85
00:03:53,729 --> 00:03:56,879
The mayor once said locals
feel caught between two towns.

86
00:03:57,549 --> 00:04:00,299
But some buildings are too
special to leave behind.

87
00:04:00,529 --> 00:04:02,959
So Kiruna does something kind of wild.

88
00:04:03,389 --> 00:04:05,539
It picks them up, and drives them away.

89
00:04:06,096 --> 00:04:08,966
Lundbohm's own house was
cut into three pieces,

90
00:04:09,056 --> 00:04:12,306
loaded onto trucks, and put back
together in the new part of town.

91
00:04:12,656 --> 00:04:14,606
Today it's a little museum with a café.

92
00:04:15,282 --> 00:04:16,632
How do you move a house, anyway?

93
00:04:17,162 --> 00:04:20,872
You disconnect the water and power,
slide huge steel beams underneath,

94
00:04:21,162 --> 00:04:23,732
jack the whole thing up,
and roll it onto a trailer.

95
00:04:24,242 --> 00:04:27,992
Then you drive very, very
slowly, and hope nobody sneezes.

96
00:04:28,534 --> 00:04:31,814
Old wooden homes rolled down
the road on giant trailers,

97
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:33,204
one at a time.

98
00:04:33,674 --> 00:04:36,744
More than twenty historic buildings
have made the trip so far.

99
00:04:37,293 --> 00:04:40,263
In twenty eighteen, the
new town hall opened.

100
00:04:40,513 --> 00:04:44,813
They call it the Crystal, because its
sharp shape copies the angles of iron

101
00:04:44,853 --> 00:04:45,423
crystals.

102
00:04:46,061 --> 00:04:48,491
And right next to it stands an old friend.

103
00:04:48,981 --> 00:04:53,461
The clock tower from the old town hall
was taken apart and rebuilt beside the new

104
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:53,891
one.

105
00:04:54,281 --> 00:04:55,851
Same clock, new address.

106
00:04:56,475 --> 00:04:58,385
The new center is still growing.

107
00:04:58,795 --> 00:05:01,885
Shops, a library,
apartments, a swimming pool.

108
00:05:02,115 --> 00:05:05,985
A whole town, built from scratch,
while people keep living in it.

109
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:12,190
Now, remember that church
Lundbohm wanted people to love?

110
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:13,410
Here it is.

111
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,590
Kiruna Church, finished
in nineteen twelve.

112
00:05:17,362 --> 00:05:20,632
Lundbohm told the architect to
build something like a Sámi hut.

113
00:05:20,822 --> 00:05:23,462
So it looks like a giant
dark-red wooden tent,

114
00:05:23,502 --> 00:05:25,972
with a roof that almost reaches the snow.

115
00:05:26,557 --> 00:05:28,547
And people really do love it.

116
00:05:28,837 --> 00:05:33,127
In two thousand one, Swedes voted it their
favorite building from before nineteen

117
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:33,647
fifty.

118
00:05:34,017 --> 00:05:35,007
In the whole country.

119
00:05:35,592 --> 00:05:37,162
So you can't knock it down.

120
00:05:37,392 --> 00:05:40,122
But you also can't leave it
sitting on top of a mine.

121
00:05:40,688 --> 00:05:44,958
So engineers spent more than a thousand
hours planning one single trip.

122
00:05:45,248 --> 00:05:46,518
About three miles.

123
00:05:46,748 --> 00:05:47,638
In one piece.

124
00:05:48,235 --> 00:05:51,105
The church weighs about six
hundred seventy-two tonnes.

125
00:05:51,575 --> 00:05:53,965
That's roughly the weight
of a hundred elephants.

126
00:05:54,712 --> 00:05:58,542
It went onto remote-controlled trailers
with two hundred twenty-four wheels.

127
00:05:58,872 --> 00:06:01,562
And the driver steered the
whole thing with a joystick,

128
00:06:01,792 --> 00:06:02,822
like a video game.

129
00:06:03,369 --> 00:06:05,839
On August nineteenth, twenty twenty-five,

130
00:06:06,409 --> 00:06:07,379
it started rolling.

131
00:06:07,809 --> 00:06:10,939
And in its first hour,
it moved, wait for it,

132
00:06:11,189 --> 00:06:12,299
about thirty meters.

133
00:06:12,975 --> 00:06:14,025
Nobody cared.

134
00:06:14,595 --> 00:06:16,625
Around ten thousand people came to watch.

135
00:06:17,195 --> 00:06:19,365
Swedish TV streamed the whole thing live,

136
00:06:19,555 --> 00:06:21,885
for hours, with dozens of cameras.

137
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:25,325
The slowest show on television,
and people loved it.

138
00:06:25,862 --> 00:06:29,642
On the second day, the church reached
its new spot near the new town center.

139
00:06:29,682 --> 00:06:32,192
And the King of Sweden
was there to welcome it.

140
00:06:32,616 --> 00:06:35,466
A hundred and thirteen
years old, three miles,

141
00:06:35,736 --> 00:06:38,546
two days, and one very patient driver.

142
00:06:38,936 --> 00:06:41,266
Then it was lowered onto
brand-new foundations.

143
00:06:44,087 --> 00:06:45,237
So that's it, right?

144
00:06:45,747 --> 00:06:48,177
Town moved, church safe, happy ending?

145
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:49,551
Not quite.

146
00:06:50,061 --> 00:06:55,341
In August twenty twenty-five, LKAB
announced that the mine affects even more of

147
00:06:55,381 --> 00:06:56,691
Kiruna than they expected.

148
00:06:57,303 --> 00:06:59,333
Another twenty-seven hundred homes.

149
00:06:59,703 --> 00:07:01,413
About six thousand more people.

150
00:07:01,683 --> 00:07:03,513
That's roughly a third of the town.

151
00:07:04,056 --> 00:07:06,146
The bill for that new area alone?

152
00:07:06,616 --> 00:07:10,066
About twenty-two and a half
billion Swedish kronor.

153
00:07:10,416 --> 00:07:12,116
More than two billion dollars.

154
00:07:12,156 --> 00:07:15,006
And the town asked the
Swedish government for help.

155
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,720
Meanwhile the old center keeps shrinking.

156
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:21,180
Some of the buildings people
pass every day are already gone,

157
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:24,220
and one by one the empty blocks come down.

158
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,410
It's not only houses, either.

159
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:31,680
The Sámi reindeer herders of Gabna say
the mine and the town have squeezed their

160
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:35,470
migration route past Kiruna
into a narrow strip of land.

161
00:07:36,025 --> 00:07:37,675
So why keep digging at all?

162
00:07:38,065 --> 00:07:41,375
Because Kiruna's iron ends
up in steel all over Europe.

163
00:07:41,765 --> 00:07:46,315
And in twenty twenty-three, LKAB found
something even bigger right next door.

164
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:50,470
Europe's largest known deposit
of rare earth elements.

165
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,890
Those are the metals
inside phone speakers,

166
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,010
electric cars and wind turbines.

167
00:07:55,740 --> 00:08:00,150
Europe badly wants its own supply, instead
of buying almost all of it from abroad.

168
00:08:00,762 --> 00:08:04,472
But mining it would also cut through
some of that last reindeer route.

169
00:08:04,842 --> 00:08:08,042
So the next chapter of Kiruna
is still being argued about,

170
00:08:08,082 --> 00:08:09,032
right now.

171
00:08:09,526 --> 00:08:12,736
So the ground under Kiruna
is worth more than ever.

172
00:08:13,066 --> 00:08:15,446
Which means this town
will probably keep moving,

173
00:08:15,486 --> 00:08:17,916
a little bit at a time, for years.

174
00:08:18,541 --> 00:08:19,531
Think about it.

175
00:08:19,881 --> 00:08:23,061
A town that was built because
of a mine is now being rebuilt,

176
00:08:23,101 --> 00:08:25,171
because of the very same mine.

177
00:08:25,561 --> 00:08:26,331
Same people.

178
00:08:26,641 --> 00:08:27,411
Same snow.

179
00:08:27,741 --> 00:08:28,951
Same northern lights.

180
00:08:29,221 --> 00:08:30,851
Just two miles down the road.

181
00:08:31,483 --> 00:08:36,533
And on the new side of town, a dark-red
wooden church stands on fresh foundations,

182
00:08:36,863 --> 00:08:39,413
getting ready for its
first winter in a new spot.

183
00:08:39,954 --> 00:08:40,944
Now I'm curious.

184
00:08:41,474 --> 00:08:43,664
If a company offered
you a brand-new house,

185
00:08:43,794 --> 00:08:45,784
but you had to leave
your old street forever,

186
00:08:46,154 --> 00:08:47,164
would you take the deal?

187
00:08:47,514 --> 00:08:48,274
Tell me in the comments.

188
00:08:48,314 --> 00:08:51,404
And tell me which strange
town we should explain next.
